# Quality Standards - Code Quality and Testing

## 📝 Code Quality Standards

### **Documentation**

- All public APIs must have docstrings
- Include parameter descriptions and return values
- Document complex logic and algorithms
- Maintain up-to-date README files

### **Type Hints**

- Use type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Include type hints for class attributes
- Use generic types where appropriate
- Validate types at runtime when necessary

### **Error Handling**

- Implement proper exception handling with meaningful messages
- Use specific exception types
- Include context information in error messages
- Log errors appropriately

### **Logging**

- Use structured logging with appropriate levels
- Include relevant context in log messages
- Avoid logging sensitive information
- Use consistent log format across the project

### **Security**

- Never hardcode secrets; use environment variables or secure config
- Validate all inputs
- Use secure coding practices
- Regular security reviews

## 🧪 Testing Standards

### **Test Coverage**

- Maintain high test coverage (minimum 80%)
- Test all public APIs
- Include edge cases and error conditions
- Test both positive and negative scenarios

### **Test Types**

- **Unit Tests** - Test individual components in isolation
- **Integration Tests** - Test component interactions
- **End-to-End Tests** - Test complete workflows
- **Performance Tests** - Test under load and stress

### **Test Quality**

- Tests should be readable and maintainable
- Use descriptive test names
- Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)
- Avoid test interdependencies

### **Test Data**

- Use realistic test data
- Avoid hardcoded test values
- Use factories for test data generation
- Clean up test data after tests

## 🔍 Code Review Standards

### **Review Checklist**

- [ ] Code follows style guidelines
- [ ] Tests are included and pass
- [ ] Documentation is updated
- [ ] Error handling is appropriate
- [ ] Performance implications considered
- [ ] Security implications reviewed

### **Review Process**

- All code changes require review
- Address all review comments
- Re-test after addressing comments
- Get approval before merging

## 📊 Quality Metrics

### **Code Metrics**

- Cyclomatic complexity
- Code duplication
- Test coverage percentage
- Documentation coverage

### **Performance Metrics**

- Response times
- Memory usage
- CPU utilization
- Error rates

### **Quality Gates**

- All tests must pass
- Coverage threshold met
- No critical security issues
- Performance benchmarks met

## 🛠️ Tools and Automation

### **Static Analysis**

- Use linters and formatters
- Run static analysis tools
- Check for security vulnerabilities
- Validate type hints

### **Continuous Integration**

- Automated testing on every commit
- Quality gates in CI pipeline
- Automated security scanning
- Performance regression testing

